{"auto_generated": false, "lang": "en", "segments": [{"duration": 0.833, "start": 0.12, "text": "- Hi there,"}, {"duration": 1.987, "start": 0.953, "text": "today, I am continuing my exploration"}, {"duration": 2.46, "start": 2.94, "text": "of security for electronics design teams"}, {"duration": 2.04, "start": 5.4, "text": "with something that's absolutely critical"}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 7.44, "text": "for anyone working in the cloud."}, {"duration": 2.04, "start": 9.96, "text": "Zero trust security implementation."}, {"duration": 1.35, "start": 12.0, "text": "Now, if you're in the\nelectronics industry,"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 13.35, "text": "you've probably noticed\nhow cybersecurity threats"}, {"duration": 2.64, "start": 15.48, "text": "are becoming more\nsophisticated every single day."}, {"duration": 1.83, "start": 18.12, "text": "Now, these old-school security methods"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 19.95, "text": "that we have used in the past"}, {"duration": 1.59, "start": 21.24, "text": "just aren't cutting it anymore."}, {"duration": 0.99, "start": 22.83, "text": "The days when you could just like,"}, {"duration": 1.95, "start": 23.82, "text": "throw up a firewall and call it a day,"}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 25.77, "text": "those are long gone."}, {"duration": 0.96, "start": 27.21, "text": "And here's why,"}, {"duration": 3.06, "start": 28.17, "text": "these traditional\nparameter-based approaches"}, {"duration": 3.0, "start": 31.23, "text": "assume that everything\ninside your network is safe,"}, {"duration": 2.76, "start": 34.23, "text": "which we know is a very\ndangerous assumption."}, {"duration": 2.94, "start": 36.99, "text": "That is why zero trust\nsecurity has become essential,"}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 39.93, "text": "especially for protecting your valuable"}, {"duration": 2.49, "start": 41.79, "text": "electronics design data in the cloud."}, {"duration": 2.46, "start": 44.28, "text": "Now, whether you are part\nof a large electronics firm"}, {"duration": 1.32, "start": 46.74, "text": "or a smaller design team,"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 48.06, "text": "implementing zero trust security"}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 49.68, "text": "could be the difference"}, {"duration": 2.61, "start": 51.24, "text": "between safeguarding your\nintellectual property"}, {"duration": 1.95, "start": 53.85, "text": "and facing a devastating breach"}, {"duration": 2.55, "start": 55.8, "text": "that has catastrophic consequences."}, {"duration": 2.46, "start": 58.35, "text": "So today, I'm gonna break down exactly"}, {"duration": 2.55, "start": 60.81, "text": "what zero trust security even is,"}, {"duration": 2.43, "start": 63.36, "text": "what it means for electronics\ndesign environments,"}, {"duration": 2.662, "start": 65.79, "text": "and how you can put it into practice."}, {"duration": 2.583, "start": 68.452, "text": "(upbeat music)"}, {"duration": 2.36, "start": 73.75, "text": "Okay, let's start with the basics,"}, {"duration": 3.03, "start": 76.11, "text": "by understanding exactly what\nzero trust security means."}, {"duration": 2.22, "start": 79.14, "text": "Now, the core concept here\nis really straightforward."}, {"duration": 1.83, "start": 81.36, "text": "Never trust, always verify."}, {"duration": 1.41, "start": 83.19, "text": "This philosophy flips"}, {"duration": 2.28, "start": 84.6, "text": "the traditional security\nmodels on their head"}, {"duration": 2.55, "start": 86.88, "text": "because those assume that devices"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 89.43, "text": "within your network are trustworthy."}, {"duration": 3.51, "start": 91.41, "text": "Zero trust requires\ncontinuous verification"}, {"duration": 2.16, "start": 94.92, "text": "of everyone and everything"}, {"duration": 2.16, "start": 97.08, "text": "attempting to access your resources,"}, {"duration": 2.37, "start": 99.24, "text": "no matter where they are coming from."}, {"duration": 1.26, "start": 101.61, "text": "For electronics design teams"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 102.87, "text": "working in cloud environments,"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 104.04, "text": "this approach is really game-changing."}, {"duration": 1.11, "start": 105.66, "text": "I mean, think about it."}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 106.77, "text": "Your designs, intellectual property,"}, {"duration": 1.02, "start": 108.9, "text": "client information,"}, {"duration": 1.8, "start": 109.92, "text": "all of this sensitive data"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 111.72, "text": "is increasingly being stored and accessed"}, {"duration": 1.8, "start": 113.85, "text": "through cloud platforms."}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 115.65, "text": "Traditional security models"}, {"duration": 2.55, "start": 117.15, "text": "were not built for this\nkind of distributed,"}, {"duration": 2.04, "start": 119.7, "text": "cloud-based working environment,"}, {"duration": 3.51, "start": 121.74, "text": "and it only takes one\nslip-up of cybersecurity"}, {"duration": 3.84, "start": 125.25, "text": "to damage everything your\norganization has built."}, {"duration": 1.8, "start": 129.09, "text": "So we need to catch up"}, {"duration": 1.83, "start": 130.89, "text": "to these cloud-based environments"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 132.72, "text": "when it comes to security, pronto."}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 134.85, "text": "So let's dive a little bit deeper."}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 136.29, "text": "What are some of the key features here"}, {"duration": 1.77, "start": 137.73, "text": "that make up zero trust security?"}, {"duration": 0.84, "start": 139.5, "text": "Well, like I said,"}, {"duration": 1.26, "start": 140.34, "text": "never trust, always verify."}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 141.6, "text": "This means every single access request"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 143.91, "text": "must be authenticated and authorized"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 145.89, "text": "regardless of where it originates from."}, {"duration": 2.1, "start": 148.02, "text": "Now, this eliminates the concept"}, {"duration": 2.46, "start": 150.12, "text": "of a \"trusted network\" entirely,"}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 152.58, "text": "and it ensures malicious actors"}, {"duration": 2.64, "start": 154.11, "text": "can't bypass your parameter defenses."}, {"duration": 2.16, "start": 156.75, "text": "Next, we got least privilege access."}, {"duration": 2.25, "start": 158.91, "text": "Users should only have access"}, {"duration": 2.43, "start": 161.16, "text": "to the specific resources they need"}, {"duration": 1.83, "start": 163.59, "text": "to do their job and nothing more."}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 165.42, "text": "For electronics design teams,"}, {"duration": 2.22, "start": 167.1, "text": "this might mean limiting access"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 169.32, "text": "to contain design files,"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 170.61, "text": "or components based off of the role"}, {"duration": 1.83, "start": 172.68, "text": "and responsibility of the\nperson within the team"}, {"duration": 1.05, "start": 174.51, "text": "that needs that information."}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 175.56, "text": "Then we've got continuous verification."}, {"duration": 2.7, "start": 177.42, "text": "Now, this is not a one-and-done process."}, {"duration": 1.65, "start": 180.12, "text": "If I could get across anything"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 181.77, "text": "when it comes to zero trust security,"}, {"duration": 0.99, "start": 183.06, "text": "it would be that."}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 184.05, "text": "Not a one-and-done process."}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 185.58, "text": "I'm probably gonna\nrepeat it multiple times"}, {"duration": 1.11, "start": 187.89, "text": "throughout the course of this video."}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 189.0, "text": "Zero trust requires ongoing"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 191.52, "text": "monitoring and authentication."}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 193.59, "text": "Systems need to constantly verify"}, {"duration": 2.49, "start": 195.9, "text": "the connected users and\ndevices to remain secure"}, {"duration": 3.24, "start": 198.39, "text": "and compliant with security policies."}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 201.63, "text": "Then you've got micro-segmentation."}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 203.31, "text": "Now, this is cool"}, {"duration": 2.017, "start": 204.143, "text": "because it involves dividing your network"}, {"duration": 1.2, "start": 206.16, "text": "into isolated segments"}, {"duration": 2.25, "start": 207.36, "text": "to limit the potential impact of a breach"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 209.61, "text": "if it were to occur."}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 211.23, "text": "If one segment is compromised,"}, {"duration": 1.77, "start": 212.73, "text": "the damage is contained there,"}, {"duration": 1.02, "start": 214.5, "text": "rather than spreading"}, {"duration": 1.77, "start": 215.52, "text": "throughout your entire system."}, {"duration": 1.23, "start": 217.29, "text": "So now let's talk a little bit"}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 218.52, "text": "about why zero trust security"}, {"duration": 1.35, "start": 220.41, "text": "is particularly important"}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 221.76, "text": "for electronics design environments."}, {"duration": 1.71, "start": 224.07, "text": "Now, the electronics industry"}, {"duration": 4.86, "start": 225.78, "text": "deals with extremely valuable\nintellectual property."}, {"duration": 0.9, "start": 230.64, "text": "Your designs,"}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 231.54, "text": "they represent a significant investment,"}, {"duration": 0.93, "start": 233.85, "text": "not just of money,"}, {"duration": 2.49, "start": 234.78, "text": "but time and expertise as well."}, {"duration": 2.04, "start": 237.27, "text": "A breach could mean losing all of that,"}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 239.31, "text": "losing your competitive advantage,"}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 240.75, "text": "compromising client data,"}, {"duration": 2.37, "start": 242.22, "text": "or even facing regulatory penalties."}, {"duration": 1.71, "start": 244.59, "text": "Additionally, electronics design"}, {"duration": 2.61, "start": 246.3, "text": "increasingly involves collaboration"}, {"duration": 2.16, "start": 248.91, "text": "with external partners, suppliers,"}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 251.07, "text": "manufacturers, contractors, et cetera."}, {"duration": 2.49, "start": 253.59, "text": "This extended network is really great,"}, {"duration": 1.08, "start": 256.08, "text": "but it does introduce"}, {"duration": 1.59, "start": 257.16, "text": "potential security vulnerabilities"}, {"duration": 2.61, "start": 258.75, "text": "that traditional parameter-based security"}, {"duration": 2.34, "start": 261.36, "text": "just can't adequately address."}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 263.7, "text": "On top of that,"}, {"duration": 1.627, "start": 264.533, "text": "the shift to cloud-based design tools"}, {"duration": 0.96, "start": 266.16, "text": "means your team members"}, {"duration": 2.61, "start": 267.12, "text": "may be accessing sensitive design data"}, {"duration": 2.16, "start": 269.73, "text": "from various locations and\ndevices around the world,"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 271.89, "text": "and you don't necessarily know"}, {"duration": 1.92, "start": 273.63, "text": "what the security protocols are"}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 275.55, "text": "in those locations and on those devices,"}, {"duration": 2.79, "start": 277.86, "text": "zero trust provides the\nflexibility you need"}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 280.65, "text": "to support this modern way of working"}, {"duration": 2.91, "start": 283.17, "text": "while maintaining rigorous\nsecurity standards"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 286.08, "text": "that are gonna protect\nyou and your organization."}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 288.06, "text": "Alright, so now we've\nexplored a little bit"}, {"duration": 1.14, "start": 289.5, "text": "of what zero trust is."}, {"duration": 1.11, "start": 290.64, "text": "Here's a big old question."}, {"duration": 2.16, "start": 291.75, "text": "How do you actually\nimplement zero trust security"}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 293.91, "text": "in an electronics design environment?"}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 295.38, "text": "Well, the first step is just to sit down"}, {"duration": 2.04, "start": 297.9, "text": "and identify your critical assets, right?"}, {"duration": 2.34, "start": 299.94, "text": "For most electronics design organizations,"}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 302.28, "text": "this will include stuff"}, {"duration": 1.207, "start": 303.113, "text": "like intellectual property,"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 304.32, "text": "design data, supply chain information,"}, {"duration": 1.59, "start": 306.39, "text": "customer data, stuff like that."}, {"duration": 2.46, "start": 307.98, "text": "Once you've figured out\nwhat these things are,"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 310.44, "text": "you build your security strategy"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 312.42, "text": "around protecting those."}, {"duration": 2.7, "start": 314.49, "text": "Next, you're gonna\nestablish a strong identity"}, {"duration": 2.43, "start": 317.19, "text": "and access management framework."}, {"duration": 2.19, "start": 319.62, "text": "This is the foundation of zero trust."}, {"duration": 2.85, "start": 321.81, "text": "It involves creating robust\nauthentication mechanisms,"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 324.66, "text": "implementing multifactor authentication,"}, {"duration": 2.64, "start": 326.73, "text": "and regularly reviewing access privileges."}, {"duration": 1.41, "start": 329.37, "text": "For electronics design teams,"}, {"duration": 1.59, "start": 330.78, "text": "this means carefully controlling"}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 332.37, "text": "who actually can access design files,"}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 334.26, "text": "simulation data,"}, {"duration": 1.087, "start": 335.093, "text": "and other sensitive information."}, {"duration": 2.7, "start": 336.18, "text": "It also means implementing\nrole-based access control,"}, {"duration": 1.92, "start": 338.88, "text": "so team members only have access"}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 340.8, "text": "to the specific resources\nthey actually need."}, {"duration": 2.34, "start": 343.32, "text": "After setting up your IAM framework,"}, {"duration": 2.58, "start": 345.66, "text": "you're gonna need to\nsecure your infrastructure."}, {"duration": 3.45, "start": 348.24, "text": "Now this involves implementing\nmicro-segmentation"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 351.69, "text": "to divide your network"}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 352.98, "text": "into smaller isolated segments."}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 354.87, "text": "For electronic design environments,"}, {"duration": 3.15, "start": 356.61, "text": "you might networks for design,"}, {"duration": 1.83, "start": 359.76, "text": "testing, manufacturing,"}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 361.59, "text": "business operations, right?"}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 363.03, "text": "Obvious segmentation there."}, {"duration": 2.7, "start": 364.56, "text": "You're also gonna need\nto employ firewalls here,"}, {"duration": 1.65, "start": 367.26, "text": "and intrusion detection systems"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 368.91, "text": "to monitor network traffic"}, {"duration": 1.59, "start": 370.53, "text": "and protect against attacks."}, {"duration": 1.11, "start": 372.12, "text": "Data encryption,"}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 373.23, "text": "both at rest and in transit,"}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 374.76, "text": "is essential for protecting"}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 376.26, "text": "sensitive design information."}, {"duration": 2.04, "start": 377.94, "text": "So you gotta get that in place as well."}, {"duration": 1.14, "start": 379.98, "text": "Another critical aspect here"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 381.12, "text": "is endpoint protection."}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 382.41, "text": "Every device that connects to your network"}, {"duration": 2.22, "start": 383.91, "text": "represents a potential entry\npoint for attacks, right?"}, {"duration": 2.25, "start": 386.13, "text": "So you need solutions that can detect"}, {"duration": 2.1, "start": 388.38, "text": "and respond to these\nthreats on these devices,"}, {"duration": 2.82, "start": 390.48, "text": "including implementing endpoint\ndetection and response,"}, {"duration": 1.59, "start": 393.3, "text": "or EDR solutions,"}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 394.89, "text": "keeping software updated,"}, {"duration": 2.91, "start": 396.36, "text": "and enforcing strong security policies."}, {"duration": 2.22, "start": 399.27, "text": "Now, supply chain security"}, {"duration": 1.32, "start": 401.49, "text": "is another critical component."}, {"duration": 0.99, "start": 402.81, "text": "We talked about it a little bit,"}, {"duration": 2.28, "start": 403.8, "text": "let's dive in a little\nbit deeper here now."}, {"duration": 3.21, "start": 406.08, "text": "Your security, it's really only as strong"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 409.29, "text": "as your weakest link,"}, {"duration": 3.48, "start": 410.46, "text": "which might be a third-party\nvendor or supplier."}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 413.94, "text": "So you're gonna have to conduct"}, {"duration": 2.01, "start": 415.41, "text": "thorough risk assessments\nwhen selecting vendors"}, {"duration": 3.51, "start": 417.42, "text": "and regularly audit their\nsecurity practices as well."}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 420.93, "text": "Implement secure software\ndevelopment lifecycles,"}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 423.06, "text": "and limit third-party vendor access"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 424.5, "text": "to sensitive information."}, {"duration": 2.67, "start": 426.24, "text": "Okay, that's a lot. (laughs)"}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 428.91, "text": "Implementing zero trust"}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 430.8, "text": "is not without its challenges,"}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 432.48, "text": "as I'm sure you're already gathering"}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 433.98, "text": "by this point of the video."}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 435.66, "text": "One of the biggest challenges is honestly,"}, {"duration": 2.79, "start": 438.18, "text": "the cultural shift that it requires."}, {"duration": 4.44, "start": 440.97, "text": "Employees may resist\nincreased security measures,"}, {"duration": 2.1, "start": 445.41, "text": "they might see them more as obstacles"}, {"duration": 2.43, "start": 447.51, "text": "rather than necessary protections."}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 449.94, "text": "So to overcome this resistance,"}, {"duration": 1.77, "start": 451.62, "text": "you're gonna need to educate your team"}, {"duration": 2.55, "start": 453.39, "text": "about why these measures\nare necessary, right?"}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 455.94, "text": "You're gonna have to help them understand"}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 458.46, "text": "the potential consequences\nof a data breach,"}, {"duration": 1.32, "start": 460.77, "text": "not just for the company,"}, {"duration": 1.23, "start": 462.09, "text": "but for their own work."}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 463.32, "text": "Nobody wants to sit down for a year,"}, {"duration": 0.84, "start": 465.45, "text": "year and a half,"}, {"duration": 3.3, "start": 466.29, "text": "and then have design work\ncompromised or stolen,"}, {"duration": 2.19, "start": 469.59, "text": "and therefore, made totally obsolete."}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 471.78, "text": "So training programs, clear communication,"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 473.67, "text": "these things go a long way toward building"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 475.29, "text": "a security-conscious culture."}, {"duration": 1.8, "start": 477.03, "text": "Another challenge here is the complexity"}, {"duration": 1.14, "start": 478.83, "text": "and cost of implementation."}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 479.97, "text": "It requires investments in technology,"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 482.49, "text": "expertise, and ongoing maintenance."}, {"duration": 3.39, "start": 484.47, "text": "However, while there is like a cost there,"}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 487.86, "text": "you really have to weigh that cost"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 489.54, "text": "against the potential financial impact"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 491.28, "text": "of a security breach,"}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 492.9, "text": "which could include direct losses,"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 494.34, "text": "reputational damage,"}, {"duration": 2.55, "start": 495.51, "text": "lost business opportunities,\nlegal liabilities."}, {"duration": 2.01, "start": 498.06, "text": "Honestly, it could pile up so much"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 500.07, "text": "that your organization\ncan no longer continue."}, {"duration": 3.45, "start": 502.05, "text": "We've seen that so many\ntimes in electronics design."}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 505.5, "text": "You don't want to be one of those people."}, {"duration": 2.34, "start": 507.0, "text": "So if you have a team\nwith limited resources"}, {"duration": 1.8, "start": 509.34, "text": "and you want to put this stuff in play,"}, {"duration": 3.36, "start": 511.14, "text": "consider starting with\nthe most critical assets,"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 514.5, "text": "and then gradually expanding."}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 516.63, "text": "This is a phased approach,"}, {"duration": 2.7, "start": 518.07, "text": "and it can make the process\nmuch more manageable."}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 520.77, "text": "Now, here's another big challenge"}, {"duration": 1.32, "start": 522.3, "text": "you're going to encounter"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 523.62, "text": "if you try to implement this stuff."}, {"duration": 2.94, "start": 525.75, "text": "That is balancing the security"}, {"duration": 1.08, "start": 528.69, "text": "that you're trying to implement"}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 529.77, "text": "with the productivity of your team."}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 531.45, "text": "Overly restrictive measures"}, {"duration": 2.16, "start": 532.74, "text": "can hinder your team's\nability to work efficiently,"}, {"duration": 3.12, "start": 534.9, "text": "and the key is to implement zero trust"}, {"duration": 2.58, "start": 538.02, "text": "in a way that provides robust protection"}, {"duration": 2.19, "start": 540.6, "text": "without creating any unnecessary friction."}, {"duration": 2.37, "start": 542.79, "text": "So well-designed user interfaces,"}, {"duration": 1.14, "start": 545.16, "text": "automated processes,"}, {"duration": 2.19, "start": 546.3, "text": "and just-in-time access can make security"}, {"duration": 1.32, "start": 548.49, "text": "as seamless as possible"}, {"duration": 1.38, "start": 549.81, "text": "from the user's perspective."}, {"duration": 0.99, "start": 551.19, "text": "So we've talked a little bit about"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 552.18, "text": "how you might implement\nzero trust security."}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 553.8, "text": "We've talked a little bit about"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 555.48, "text": "a phased approach,"}, {"duration": 1.11, "start": 556.65, "text": "we've talked a little bit about"}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 557.76, "text": "what might happen if you don't,"}, {"duration": 1.2, "start": 559.29, "text": "and why you really should."}, {"duration": 3.39, "start": 560.49, "text": "Now let's talk about specific\ntechnology and tools."}, {"duration": 1.05, "start": 563.88, "text": "And before I get into that,"}, {"duration": 3.21, "start": 564.93, "text": "I do want to say that\ndown in the description,"}, {"duration": 2.4, "start": 568.14, "text": "you're gonna find an\narticle that's going to have"}, {"duration": 3.72, "start": 570.54, "text": "much more comprehensive information about"}, {"duration": 1.05, "start": 574.26, "text": "everything I'm about to say"}, {"duration": 1.2, "start": 575.31, "text": "from this point on the video."}, {"duration": 1.8, "start": 576.51, "text": "So be sure to check that out."}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 578.31, "text": "And while you're scrolling down,"}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 580.2, "text": "why don't you go ahead\nand hit that Like button,"}, {"duration": 1.32, "start": 581.76, "text": "hit that Subscribe button,"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 583.08, "text": "hit the notification bell"}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 584.25, "text": "if you want to be kept up to date"}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 586.11, "text": "with all the things we're\ndoing on this channel."}, {"duration": 2.4, "start": 587.67, "text": "We talk about PCB design,\nelectronics design,"}, {"duration": 2.22, "start": 590.07, "text": "security, supply chain, everything."}, {"duration": 1.92, "start": 592.29, "text": "We got content coming\nout every single weekday,"}, {"duration": 1.2, "start": 594.21, "text": "you want to be a part of it,"}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 595.41, "text": "Hit the sub right now."}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 596.85, "text": "On the subject of tools,"}, {"duration": 1.77, "start": 598.47, "text": "for identity and access management,"}, {"duration": 2.4, "start": 600.24, "text": "consider solutions like\nOkta, Ping Identity,"}, {"duration": 2.64, "start": 602.64, "text": "or Microsoft Azure Active Directory."}, {"duration": 2.91, "start": 605.28, "text": "These platforms are gonna\nhelp manage user identities,"}, {"duration": 1.8, "start": 608.19, "text": "implement multifactor authentication,"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 609.99, "text": "and control access to resources."}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 611.61, "text": "For network security tools,"}, {"duration": 2.82, "start": 613.5, "text": "think about Cisco Zero\nTrust Network Access,"}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 616.32, "text": "Zscaler Private Access,"}, {"duration": 1.92, "start": 617.88, "text": "Palo Alto Networks Prisma Access,"}, {"duration": 2.4, "start": 619.8, "text": "all these are gonna help\nimplement micro-segmentation"}, {"duration": 2.82, "start": 622.2, "text": "and secure access to applications."}, {"duration": 1.8, "start": 625.02, "text": "And then for endpoint protection,"}, {"duration": 1.95, "start": 626.82, "text": "look into solutions\nlike CrowdStrike Falcon,"}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 628.77, "text": "Microsoft Defender for Endpoint,"}, {"duration": 0.87, "start": 630.27, "text": "or SentinelOne."}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 631.14, "text": "These tools are gonna help detect"}, {"duration": 2.28, "start": 632.58, "text": "and respond to threats\non endpoint devices."}, {"duration": 2.28, "start": 634.86, "text": "Data protection solutions like Vera"}, {"duration": 1.65, "start": 637.14, "text": "or Microsoft Information Protection"}, {"duration": 2.73, "start": 638.79, "text": "can also help protect\nsensitive design data"}, {"duration": 2.46, "start": 641.52, "text": "through encryption and access controls"}, {"duration": 1.26, "start": 643.98, "text": "that stay with the data"}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 645.24, "text": "no matter where it goes."}, {"duration": 1.41, "start": 646.68, "text": "For monitoring and analytics,"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 648.09, "text": "you could look at Splunk,"}, {"duration": 2.73, "start": 649.26, "text": "Microsoft Sentinel, IBM Qradar,"}, {"duration": 3.09, "start": 651.99, "text": "these all provide visibility\ninto your environment."}, {"duration": 1.65, "start": 655.08, "text": "They detect potential threats,"}, {"duration": 2.73, "start": 656.73, "text": "and enable quick responses\nto security incidents."}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 659.46, "text": "But again, I just want to point out here,"}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 661.02, "text": "remember, zero trust is not about"}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 663.54, "text": "just deploying a technology,"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 665.07, "text": "and forgetting that you employed it,"}, {"duration": 1.26, "start": 666.36, "text": "and assuming you're safe."}, {"duration": 2.49, "start": 667.62, "text": "It is really about a\ncomprehensive approach"}, {"duration": 2.4, "start": 670.11, "text": "that includes people,\nprocesses, and technology."}, {"duration": 2.76, "start": 672.51, "text": "So let's get all of this into practice."}, {"duration": 2.49, "start": 675.27, "text": "Let's explore a real-world example."}, {"duration": 2.97, "start": 677.76, "text": "Imagine you are a part of a design team,"}, {"duration": 2.22, "start": 680.73, "text": "and you're working on a new IOT device."}, {"duration": 3.93, "start": 682.95, "text": "It's a Ring camera that\nsits in your refrigerator,"}, {"duration": 3.27, "start": 686.88, "text": "and every time you go in to get a snack"}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 690.15, "text": "past 10:00 PM at night,"}, {"duration": 1.77, "start": 692.04, "text": "it broadcasts your face"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 693.81, "text": "getting the food out of the fridge"}, {"duration": 2.88, "start": 695.79, "text": "to all of your friends on social media."}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 698.67, "text": "Okay, so you're building this device"}, {"duration": 1.71, "start": 700.23, "text": "and you're collaborating with colleagues"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 701.94, "text": "in different locations,"}, {"duration": 2.28, "start": 703.23, "text": "external partners to get\nall the components together."}, {"duration": 2.55, "start": 705.51, "text": "In a traditional security model,"}, {"duration": 2.67, "start": 708.06, "text": "once someone got access to your network,"}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 710.73, "text": "they might be able to access"}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 712.23, "text": "all your design files, right?"}, {"duration": 1.35, "start": 713.7, "text": "This includes your sensitive IP"}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 715.05, "text": "that maybe you got"}, {"duration": 2.407, "start": 715.883, "text": "from like the camera manufacturer"}, {"duration": 2.91, "start": 718.29, "text": "that you're going to put\ninto your new IOT device."}, {"duration": 1.05, "start": 721.2, "text": "But with zero trust,"}, {"duration": 1.2, "start": 722.25, "text": "if you have that in place,"}, {"duration": 1.2, "start": 723.45, "text": "it's completely different."}, {"duration": 1.71, "start": 724.65, "text": "Every user is gonna have to authenticate"}, {"duration": 1.83, "start": 726.36, "text": "their identity using strong credentials,"}, {"duration": 2.4, "start": 728.19, "text": "potentially including\nmultifactor authentication."}, {"duration": 2.28, "start": 730.59, "text": "And this verification is\ngonna continuously happen"}, {"duration": 1.2, "start": 732.87, "text": "throughout their entire session."}, {"duration": 2.61, "start": 734.07, "text": "You're also gonna be able to set access"}, {"duration": 4.05, "start": 736.68, "text": "to specific resources\nbased off of privileges"}, {"duration": 0.93, "start": 740.73, "text": "that you provide,"}, {"duration": 2.22, "start": 741.66, "text": "and the principles of least privilege."}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 743.88, "text": "Now, hardware designer, right?"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 745.35, "text": "The person who's actually making"}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 747.09, "text": "the box or whatever,"}, {"duration": 1.77, "start": 748.77, "text": "is probably gonna have access to,"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 750.54, "text": "you know, schematic files,"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 751.71, "text": "but not necessarily like firmware code."}, {"duration": 1.11, "start": 753.84, "text": "The manufacturing partner,"}, {"duration": 1.95, "start": 754.95, "text": "who's gonna make your weird little box,"}, {"duration": 2.4, "start": 756.9, "text": "might be able to access\nthe production files"}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 759.3, "text": "to make your weird little box,"}, {"duration": 2.94, "start": 760.83, "text": "but not early design stage documents"}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 763.77, "text": "and your network is segmented,"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 765.21, "text": "so that unauthorized access to one part"}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 767.34, "text": "doesn't enable lateral movement"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 769.02, "text": "across other resources,"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 770.76, "text": "and lateral movement across resources"}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 772.83, "text": "is a really good way to frame it, I think."}, {"duration": 2.46, "start": 775.35, "text": "all your traffic across your design team"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 777.81, "text": "is gonna be inspected and logged,"}, {"duration": 2.76, "start": 779.94, "text": "and this allows for real-time monitoring."}, {"duration": 2.25, "start": 782.7, "text": "Data is encrypted both\nin rest and at transit,"}, {"duration": 3.0, "start": 784.95, "text": "so if you are sending\nover your design files"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 787.95, "text": "to somebody in Vietnam"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 789.93, "text": "that you want to look at to figure out"}, {"duration": 2.64, "start": 791.67, "text": "how to do face recognition or something"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 794.31, "text": "using edge device,"}, {"duration": 1.41, "start": 795.48, "text": "I don't know, whatever,"}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 796.89, "text": "it's gonna be protected,"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 798.39, "text": "even if it's intercepted on its way there."}, {"duration": 1.38, "start": 800.46, "text": "And all this happens seamlessly"}, {"duration": 1.35, "start": 801.84, "text": "for legitimate users,"}, {"duration": 1.14, "start": 803.19, "text": "allowing efficient work"}, {"duration": 1.59, "start": 804.33, "text": "while maintaining strong security."}, {"duration": 3.39, "start": 805.92, "text": "Now we're pretty far into\nour exploration here,"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 809.31, "text": "but I want to really hammer\nsomething down, right?"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 811.29, "text": "Because I know that a lot of people"}, {"duration": 1.92, "start": 813.27, "text": "who will be watching these videos"}, {"duration": 2.67, "start": 815.19, "text": "who are curious about\nzero trust implementation"}, {"duration": 2.46, "start": 817.86, "text": "are gonna be coming from\nsmaller design teams,"}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 820.32, "text": "and they want to implement this stuff,"}, {"duration": 2.67, "start": 821.85, "text": "and they're curious about\nthis phased approach."}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 824.52, "text": "So let me break down beyond,"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 826.65, "text": "just conceptually what you would do"}, {"duration": 1.11, "start": 828.39, "text": "in a phased approach."}, {"duration": 2.28, "start": 829.5, "text": "Let me talk about more specifically"}, {"duration": 3.0, "start": 831.78, "text": "the things you might do in each phase."}, {"duration": 2.64, "start": 834.78, "text": "So, phase one of implementation,"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 837.42, "text": "this is really gonna be used"}, {"duration": 3.9, "start": 838.59, "text": "to establish strong identity\nand access management"}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 842.49, "text": "with multifactor authentication,"}, {"duration": 3.57, "start": 844.38, "text": "single sign-on, and\nrole-based access control."}, {"duration": 1.02, "start": 847.95, "text": "That's phase one."}, {"duration": 1.41, "start": 848.97, "text": "You get that locked down,"}, {"duration": 1.59, "start": 850.38, "text": "you're a lot of the way there."}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 851.97, "text": "You're way more secure than you were"}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 853.71, "text": "when you started."}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 854.543, "text": "Phase two,"}, {"duration": 1.814, "start": 855.376, "text": "okay, now we're gonna go into the network."}, {"duration": 1.41, "start": 857.19, "text": "We're gonna segment the network,"}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 858.6, "text": "we're gonna put in encryption,"}, {"duration": 0.84, "start": 860.46, "text": "and we're going to make sure"}, {"duration": 1.95, "start": 861.3, "text": "we have enhanced monitoring."}, {"duration": 2.1, "start": 863.25, "text": "And again, we're just building out"}, {"duration": 1.77, "start": 865.35, "text": "from our critical assets, right?"}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 867.12, "text": "We started with all of our sign-on stuff,"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 869.64, "text": "our user access stuff,"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 870.93, "text": "now we are building out into network."}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 872.55, "text": "So now phase three,"}, {"duration": 1.35, "start": 874.29, "text": "we're gonna go ahead and focus"}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 875.64, "text": "on endpoint security."}, {"duration": 1.95, "start": 877.2, "text": "We're gonna make sure all devices"}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 879.15, "text": "meet security requirements,"}, {"duration": 2.46, "start": 880.62, "text": "and that they are also\ncontinuously monitored."}, {"duration": 1.35, "start": 883.08, "text": "And then phase four,"}, {"duration": 2.1, "start": 884.43, "text": "we're gonna look at data protection,"}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 886.53, "text": "encryption, access controls"}, {"duration": 2.25, "start": 888.39, "text": "to protect sensitive design information"}, {"duration": 1.02, "start": 890.64, "text": "throughout the lifecycle,"}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 891.66, "text": "all that stuff."}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 892.493, "text": "And then phase five,"}, {"duration": 1.664, "start": 893.326, "text": "we've ballooned out the most."}, {"duration": 1.65, "start": 894.99, "text": "Now we're looking at supply chain,"}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 896.64, "text": "we're vetting our vendors,"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 898.11, "text": "we're limiting third party access,"}, {"duration": 2.25, "start": 899.85, "text": "we are ensuring component security."}, {"duration": 2.64, "start": 902.1, "text": "Again, I said I was gonna\nreiterate at the top,"}, {"duration": 1.17, "start": 904.74, "text": "I'm reiterating it now."}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 905.91, "text": "This is not a one-and-done\nthing, it's ongoing."}, {"duration": 2.25, "start": 908.22, "text": "The threat landscape\nis constantly evolving,"}, {"duration": 1.26, "start": 910.47, "text": "so your security approach"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 911.73, "text": "has to evolve alongside with it,"}, {"duration": 1.02, "start": 913.35, "text": "because of that,"}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 914.37, "text": "regular security assessments"}, {"duration": 2.01, "start": 916.23, "text": "to figure out where the gaps are,"}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 918.24, "text": "is gonna be really\ncrucial for your success."}, {"duration": 2.52, "start": 920.1, "text": "User access privileges, this is a big one,"}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 922.62, "text": "need to be looked at all the time"}, {"duration": 2.34, "start": 924.51, "text": "to make sure that those\naccess requirements"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 926.85, "text": "actually fit with current roles."}, {"duration": 3.6, "start": 928.92, "text": "This is like something\nyou see all the time."}, {"duration": 1.41, "start": 932.52, "text": "People with access roles"}, {"duration": 1.71, "start": 933.93, "text": "from projects they did two years ago,"}, {"duration": 1.71, "start": 935.64, "text": "you got to make sure that does not happen."}, {"duration": 1.83, "start": 937.35, "text": "Now I want to be honest here and talk,"}, {"duration": 2.43, "start": 939.18, "text": "we talked a little bit\nabout challenges earlier."}, {"duration": 1.23, "start": 941.61, "text": "I want to talk a little bit about"}, {"duration": 2.82, "start": 942.84, "text": "just sort of common questions and concerns"}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 945.66, "text": "that you get when you're talking about"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 947.22, "text": "implementing zero trust security."}, {"duration": 1.2, "start": 948.96, "text": "The the big one is that"}, {"duration": 2.25, "start": 950.16, "text": "it's gonna slow down design processes."}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 952.41, "text": "Okay, I'm not gonna lie,"}, {"duration": 2.64, "start": 954.09, "text": "while any additional security measures"}, {"duration": 2.76, "start": 956.73, "text": "could potentially introduce friction,"}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 959.49, "text": "well-designed systems,"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 961.17, "text": "they really do aim to make security"}, {"duration": 3.21, "start": 963.24, "text": "as seamless as possible\nfor legitimate users."}, {"duration": 3.12, "start": 966.45, "text": "The next big consideration\nis obviously the cost."}, {"duration": 2.88, "start": 969.57, "text": "There are investments to be made here,"}, {"duration": 1.05, "start": 972.45, "text": "it's true,"}, {"duration": 1.35, "start": 973.5, "text": "but again, you got to weigh those"}, {"duration": 2.49, "start": 974.85, "text": "against the potential cost of loss"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 977.34, "text": "due to a data breach."}, {"duration": 1.657, "start": 978.63, "text": "Another concern you\nhear regularly is like,"}, {"duration": 3.473, "start": 980.287, "text": "\"Well, if you implement\nthis zero trust stuff,"}, {"duration": 2.91, "start": 983.76, "text": "wouldn't that hinder your\nability to collaborate"}, {"duration": 1.95, "start": 986.67, "text": "with external partners?\""}, {"duration": 2.7, "start": 988.62, "text": "That is a super legitimate concern"}, {"duration": 1.83, "start": 991.32, "text": "in an industry where collaboration"}, {"duration": 2.01, "start": 993.15, "text": "is as common as it is in this one."}, {"duration": 2.58, "start": 995.16, "text": "However, zero trust doesn't mean no trust,"}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 997.74, "text": "it just means verifying trust"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 999.6, "text": "before granting access."}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 1000.89, "text": "So at the right systems,"}, {"duration": 1.65, "start": 1002.18, "text": "you can enable secure collaboration"}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 1003.83, "text": "while protecting all of\nyour sensitive design data."}, {"duration": 1.35, "start": 1006.14, "text": "And on top of just the peace of mind"}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 1007.49, "text": "that you're gonna get"}, {"duration": 1.297, "start": 1008.323, "text": "from putting these protections in place,"}, {"duration": 1.14, "start": 1009.62, "text": "you're also gonna be much closer"}, {"duration": 2.64, "start": 1010.76, "text": "to any regulatory compliances\nthat you need to meet."}, {"duration": 1.32, "start": 1013.4, "text": "If you want to know more about those,"}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 1014.72, "text": "again, check out the\nlink in the description."}, {"duration": 1.38, "start": 1016.25, "text": "One thing I will mention though,"}, {"duration": 1.95, "start": 1017.63, "text": "about regulatory compliances,"}, {"duration": 1.74, "start": 1019.58, "text": "is some regulations are beginning"}, {"duration": 1.65, "start": 1021.32, "text": "to specifically recognize"}, {"duration": 3.03, "start": 1022.97, "text": "or require zero trust approaches."}, {"duration": 1.08, "start": 1026.0, "text": "One you might want to look at"}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 1027.08, "text": "is the US Government's executive order"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 1028.94, "text": "on improving the nation's cybersecurity,"}, {"duration": 0.9, "start": 1031.01, "text": "for example."}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 1031.91, "text": "I think regardless of how you are thinking"}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 1033.89, "text": "about zero trust implementation"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 1036.2, "text": "or your electronics design team,"}, {"duration": 1.77, "start": 1038.27, "text": "one thing that is for sure,"}, {"duration": 2.94, "start": 1040.04, "text": "is that as design tools and workflows"}, {"duration": 3.69, "start": 1042.98, "text": "continue moving up and out into the cloud,"}, {"duration": 1.65, "start": 1046.67, "text": "we're all gonna need more robust"}, {"duration": 2.91, "start": 1048.32, "text": "and flexible security\napproaches like zero trust."}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 1051.23, "text": "We're likely gonna see, you know,"}, {"duration": 2.28, "start": 1052.85, "text": "greater integration of\nzero trust principles"}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 1055.13, "text": "into design platforms and tools."}, {"duration": 1.62, "start": 1056.75, "text": "And one thing I've not brought up here"}, {"duration": 2.34, "start": 1058.37, "text": "that is a big player, is AI."}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 1060.71, "text": "AI and machine learning,"}, {"duration": 1.98, "start": 1062.39, "text": "they are gonna play an increasing role."}, {"duration": 1.71, "start": 1064.37, "text": "They're gonna be used to help identify"}, {"duration": 1.23, "start": 1066.08, "text": "and access patterns"}, {"duration": 2.01, "start": 1067.31, "text": "that might indicate security threats,"}, {"duration": 0.833, "start": 1069.32, "text": "huge deal."}, {"duration": 2.767, "start": 1070.153, "text": "Also, your weird little refrigerator box"}, {"duration": 2.67, "start": 1072.92, "text": "that shames you for eating late at night"}, {"duration": 2.13, "start": 1075.59, "text": "is an IOT device, right?"}, {"duration": 3.57, "start": 1077.72, "text": "And those also present\nboth a lot of challenges"}, {"duration": 1.05, "start": 1081.29, "text": "and a lot of opportunities"}, {"duration": 1.71, "start": 1082.34, "text": "as electronics companies design"}, {"duration": 2.31, "start": 1084.05, "text": "more connected devices like that,"}, {"duration": 1.86, "start": 1086.36, "text": "they need to implement\nzero trust principles,"}, {"duration": 1.68, "start": 1088.22, "text": "not just in their design environments,"}, {"duration": 1.32, "start": 1089.9, "text": "but the products themselves,"}, {"duration": 1.29, "start": 1091.22, "text": "because you know,"}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 1092.51, "text": "you want to broadcast your shame"}, {"duration": 1.2, "start": 1093.98, "text": "to your friends and family,"}, {"duration": 1.02, "start": 1095.18, "text": "not to strangers."}, {"duration": 1.53, "start": 1096.2, "text": "So I hope that this information"}, {"duration": 1.5, "start": 1097.73, "text": "about zero trust was helpful."}, {"duration": 1.081, "start": 1099.23, "text": "The big thing to remember here"}, {"duration": 2.249, "start": 1100.311, "text": "is that it is a marathon, not a sprint."}, {"duration": 0.96, "start": 1102.56, "text": "Take it one step at a time"}, {"duration": 1.44, "start": 1103.52, "text": "if you're implementing this stuff,"}, {"duration": 1.56, "start": 1104.96, "text": "focus on critical assets first."}, {"duration": 0.84, "start": 1106.52, "text": "Build out from there."}, {"duration": 2.55, "start": 1107.36, "text": "If you found this information valuable,"}, {"duration": 2.37, "start": 1109.91, "text": "please do go ahead and\ngive the video a thumbs-up."}, {"duration": 1.47, "start": 1112.28, "text": "Subscribe for more content"}, {"duration": 1.41, "start": 1113.75, "text": "on electronics design security,"}, {"duration": 1.92, "start": 1115.16, "text": "electronics design in general,"}, {"duration": 2.07, "start": 1117.08, "text": "supply chain stuff, all sort of stuff."}, {"duration": 1.89, "start": 1119.15, "text": "Thanks so much for watching this video."}, {"duration": 1.055, "start": 1121.04, "text": "I'll see you in the next one."}, {"duration": 2.583, "start": 1122.095, "text": "(upbeat music)"}], "source": "innertube", "videoId": "X26qHh2VdMA", "video_id": "X26qHh2VdMA", "title": "Overview: Zero Trust Security Implementation for Electronics Design"}